From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:19:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] block: test that a raw image keeps its size after a discard
 or write-zeroes at the disk's end

imago's File storage (0.2.3) served a discard, unmap write-zeroes or plain
write-zeroes whose range reaches the end of the file by truncating the file
to the start of the range (File::try_discard_by_truncate). For a raw image
the file length is the disk size, so the disk shrank: the guest kept the old
capacity until it was restarted, then saw a smaller device than the
filesystem on it. mke2fs zeroes the last 64 KiB of the device it formats
(old MD RAID superblock wipe), so a whole-disk ext4 made in the guest lost
exactly 64 KiB of image and failed to mount on the next boot ("filesystem
larger than device"); fstrim/blkdiscard of a whole-disk filesystem whose
last blocks are free does the same. A GPT disk such as steamos.img is not
hit in practice: the backup GPT occupies the last sectors, so no partition
discard reaches the end of the file.

Upstream state: fixed in imago 0.2.5 (hreitz/imago d48b76e1 "file: keep
image size after tail discard"); patch 0025 takes imago 0.2.6 (libkrun
d166df9a). This adds the regression test only; no code change.

Test: virtio::block::device::tests::
raw_image_keeps_size_after_tail_discard_and_write_zeroes opens a raw image
through Block::new, sends write-zeroes, unmap write-zeroes and discard for
the last 64 KiB, and checks the file size and the capacity on reopen. Fails
on imago 0.2.3 (4194304 -> 4128768 bytes), passes on 0.2.5 and 0.2.6.

[steamac sync 1.9.14: fork patch 0027 bumped imago to 0.2.5 itself; upstream
0025 (imago 0.2.6) replaces that bump, the test is kept.]
---
 src/devices/src/virtio/block/device.rs | 52 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 52 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/devices/src/virtio/block/device.rs b/src/devices/src/virtio/block/device.rs
index 9e83a77..81aefb1 100644
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/block/device.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/block/device.rs
@@ -494,6 +494,58 @@ mod tests {
         );
     }
 
+    /// A raw image is the disk: a discard or write-zeroes request that reaches the end of the
+    /// device must not shorten the file, or the next boot sees a smaller disk than the
+    /// filesystem on it (mke2fs zeroes the last 64 KiB of the device; fstrim and blkdiscard
+    /// on a whole-disk filesystem end there too).
+    #[test]
+    fn raw_image_keeps_size_after_tail_discard_and_write_zeroes() {
+        const SIZE: u64 = 4 << 20;
+        const TAIL: u64 = 64 << 10;
+        let backing = TempFile::new().expect("create backing file");
+        let path = backing.as_path().to_str().unwrap().to_string();
+        let open = || {
+            Block::new(
+                "tail".to_string(),
+                None,
+                CacheType::Unsafe,
+                path.clone(),
+                ImageType::Raw,
+                false,
+                false,
+                SyncMode::Full,
+            )
+            .expect("open raw image")
+        };
+
+        for request in ["write-zeroes", "write-zeroes+unmap", "discard"] {
+            backing.as_file().set_len(SIZE).expect("size backing file");
+            let block = open();
+            assert_eq!({ block.config.capacity }, SIZE / SECTOR_SIZE);
+            {
+                let mut disk = block.disk_image.lock().unwrap();
+                match request {
+                    "write-zeroes" => disk.write_zeroes(SIZE - TAIL, TAIL),
+                    "write-zeroes+unmap" => disk.discard_to_zero(SIZE - TAIL, TAIL),
+                    _ => disk.discard_to_any(SIZE - TAIL, TAIL),
+                }
+                .expect(request);
+            }
+            drop(block);
+
+            assert_eq!(
+                backing.as_file().metadata().unwrap().len(),
+                SIZE,
+                "{request} at the end of the disk changed the image file size"
+            );
+            assert_eq!(
+                { open().config.capacity },
+                SIZE / SECTOR_SIZE,
+                "{request} at the end of the disk shrank the disk seen on the next open"
+            );
+        }
+    }
+
     #[test]
     fn disk_image_id_accepts_empty_block_id() {
         let backing = TempFile::new().expect("create backing file");
-- 
